---
import CortexInfoLayout from '../../layouts/CortexInfoLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const effectiveDate = 'August 11, 2026';
---

<CortexInfoLayout
  title={`Cortex Privacy Policy - ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="How Cortex stores game data locally and uses optional Apple Game Center and iCloud services."
  path="/cortex/privacy"
  heading="Cortex Privacy Policy"
  intro="Cortex is designed to keep your games and their history close to you, with no Nintek account or backend."
  current="privacy"
  effectiveDate={effectiveDate}
  effectiveDateTime="2026-08-11"
>
  <p class="cx-info-summary">
    <strong>In short:</strong> Cortex is an iOS-only, local-first hub of eight games.
    Nintek operates no Cortex backend and does not receive your gameplay history.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="information-cortex-stores">
    <h2 id="information-cortex-stores">Information Cortex stores</h2>
    <p>
      Cortex stores your gameplay progress, app and game settings, and detailed play
      statistics locally on your iPhone or iPad. This information supports features
      such as resuming games, remembering preferences, and showing your history.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because Nintek does not operate a Cortex backend, this locally stored
      information is not sent to or stored by Nintek.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="optional-apple-services">
    <h2 id="optional-apple-services">Optional Apple services</h2>

    <h3>Game Center</h3>
    <p>
      Game Center is optional. When you sign in to Game Center, Apple handles your
      Apple player identity and receives scores, leaderboard entries, and achievements
      that Cortex submits. Apple processes that information under
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a> and
      applicable terms.
    </p>

    <h3>Sudoku iCloud sync</h3>
    <p>
      Sudoku may use Apple's iCloud key-value storage to keep its sync data available
      across devices signed in to the same Apple Account. This sync is provided by
      Apple, not a Nintek backend, and is subject to Apple's terms and privacy
      practices.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="information-cortex-does-not-collect">
    <h2 id="information-cortex-does-not-collect">What Cortex does not do</h2>
    <p>Cortex has:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising.</li>
      <li>No third-party analytics.</li>
      <li>No cross-app tracking.</li>
      <li>No sale of personal data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-choices">
    <h2 id="privacy-choices">Your choices and data deletion</h2>
    <p>
      You can manage Game Center and iCloud from Apple Settings on your device.
      Settings may also be used to change the Apple Account associated with those
      services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting Cortex removes the gameplay progress, settings, and detailed play
      statistics stored locally by the app. Data held by Apple through Game Center or
      iCloud is managed separately through Apple's settings and services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="policy-changes">
    <h2 id="policy-changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If Cortex's data practices change, Nintek will update this policy and its
      effective date. The effective date of this policy is {effectiveDate}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-contact">
    <h2 id="privacy-contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For help with Cortex, visit <a href="/cortex/support">Cortex Support</a>. For
      privacy questions, email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}?subject=Cortex%20Privacy`}>
        {COMPANY.privacyEmail}
      </a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</CortexInfoLayout>
